invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20.c's use_avx2 answers 0 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu says,
  so no session runs the AVX2 kernel and CH_CPU_AVX2 picks nothing. Every
  vector passes, because the SSE2 path computes the same bytes; only the
  time is wrong. The script compiles chacha20.c for x86-64 and requires
  chacha20_xor_cpu to call the kernel.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 0;
